  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Controlled Tabs",
      "text": "To control Tabs state, use `value` and `onChange` props:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Uncontrolled Tabs",
      "text": "If you do not need to subscribe to Tabs state changes, use `defaultValue`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Change colors",
      "text": "To change colors of all tabs, set `color` on `Tabs` component, to change color of the individual tab,\nset `color` on `Tabs.Tab`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tabs position",
      "text": "To display tab on the opposite side, set `margin-left: auto` with `ml=\"auto\"` prop or with `className`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inverted tabs",
      "text": "To make tabs inverted, place `Tabs.Panel` components before `Tabs.List` and add `inverted` prop to `Tabs` component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Vertical tabs placement",
      "text": "To change placement of `Tabs.List` in vertical orientation set `placement` prop:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Custom variants",
      "text": "Example of custom variant with [FloatingIndicator](/core/floating-indicator):",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disabled tabs",
      "text": "Set `disabled` prop on `Tabs.Tab` component to disable tab.\nDisabled tab cannot be activated with mouse or keyboard, and they will be skipped when user navigates with arrow keys:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Activation mode",
      "text": "By default, tabs are activated when user presses arrows keys or Home/End keys.\nTo disable that set `activateTabWithKeyboard={false}` on `Tabs` component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Tab deactivation",
      "text": "By default, active tab cannot be deactivated. To allow that set `allowTabDeactivation` on `Tabs` component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Unmount inactive tabs",
      "text": "By default, inactive `Tabs.Panel` will stay mounted, to unmount inactive tabs, set `keepMounted={false}` on Tabs.\nThis is useful when you want to render components that impact performance inside `Tabs.Panel`. Note that\ncomponents that are rendered inside `Tabs.Panel` will reset their state on each mount (tab change).",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Usage with Next.js router",
      "text": "Example of Styles API usage to customize tab styles:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "Tabs component follows [WAI-ARIA recommendations](https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-practices/examples/tabs/tabs-2/tabs.html) on accessibility.\n\nIf you use `Tabs.Tab` without text content, for example, only with icon, then set `aria-label`\nor use [VisuallyHidden](/core/visually-hidden) component:\n\nTo set tabs list label, set `aria-label` on `Tabs.List` component, it will be announced by screen reader:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Keyboard interactions",
      "text": "  data={[\n\n      key: 'ArrowRight',\n      description:\n        'Focuses and activates next tab that is not disabled',\n      condition: 'orientation=\"horizontal\"',\n    },\n\n      key: 'ArrowLeft',\n      description:\n        'Focuses and activates previous tab that is not disabled',\n      condition: 'orientation=\"horizontal\"',\n    },\n\n      key: 'ArrowDown',\n      description:\n        'Focuses and activates next tab that is not disabled',\n      condition: 'orientation=\"vertical\"',\n    },\n\n      key: 'ArrowUp',\n      description:\n        'Focuses and activates previous tab that is not disabled',\n      condition: 'orientation=\"vertical\"',\n    },\n\n  ]}\n/>",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
